A||||4||XDrewX||How much Paint will it take ?||||2||
Z||000000||XDrewX||11-25-2001||12:15 AM||||How much paint will it take to paint a Fiero,  This would include painting under the hood and trunk.<P>Thanks<P>Andrew||||reg||2
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-25-2001||12:59 AM||||I paint all my cars. Usually only takes one quart...but keep in mind, when you add the reducers and what not, it comes out to be two quarts sprayable. I usually dont paint under the hoods though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-25-2001||07:31 AM||||Normaly under the hood & decklid also the door jambs are black. Unless you want otherwise.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.tripod.com/wawoonigootphet/images/af/3in1_vu1.jpg">  <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-25-2001||07:46 PM||||If im painting it back same color, 1 qt of paint , 1 quart of clear. May take more if your changing the color, like from white to black. 2 coats of base color is usally enough, 2 coats of clear with an extra coat on hood and decklid so you can wet sand and rub out.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroX||11-26-2001||03:31 AM||||I went from blue to white on my car and I used a little over 1.5 quarts (3 sprayable) and 2 quarts (1 gallon sprayable) of clearcoat.  I sprayed 4 coats of base and 4 coats of clear. I didnt paint under the decklid, hood or anything, just in the 1" of door jamb and the insides of the fenders and quarters.  Its best to always have too much than not enough so buy 2 quarts of base and 2 quarts of clear.  <BR>I used to work at a hot rod shop about 2 years back, and my boss was doing a chromalusion job on a nissan (all riced out) and he ran out of color with only a minimal amount remaining to finish.  It was a weekend and the only place open was 30 miles away.  He drove there, paid $315 for a pint of paint, and drove back to finish the job.  It turned out real nice, but it was a major hassle having to shut everything down and make an hour round trip to buy material to finish the job.  maybe he shouldnt of been such a cheapskate.  (thats another story)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
